# (docs/research/double-battles.md §6.3): two trainers against the player
# alone, type 19, by sight. A constructed system replay (party and warp setup lines, no story chain): Eterna Forest
# row 67, Psychic Lindsey at 50 facing right and Psychic Elijah at 55 facing left, both with sight 4. Stepping up
# onto 52, 67 both see the player; with two Pokémon that can fight the field makes it APPROACH_TYPE_VS2 (decomp
# FieldSystem_CheckForTrainersWantingBattle), both walk up, and the common script starts the trainer battle with
# the two ids and no partner (decomp Encounter_NewVsTrainer: TAG_DOUBLES, 19): each trainer's Pokémon from its own
# party (the owner adapter). Runs headless in tests/integration/m5-doubles.rom.test.ts.
party 0 platinum:SPECIES_STARAVIA 25
party 1 platinum:SPECIES_MONFERNO 25
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_ETERNA_FOREST 52 69 up
until idle
+0 press up
until position 52 67
+0 release up
advance text 3000
battle auto 30000
+0 assert battle trainer platinum:TRAINER_PSYCHIC_LINDSEY won trainer-pair
+0 assert battle trainer platinum:TRAINER_PSYCHIC_ELIJAH won trainer-pair
advance text 3000
until idle 3000
